$DIR/main.p:15:10: v was moved into eat (its parameter takes an owned[L] by value) at line 138, so it can no longer be used here
    owned[L] is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when
    they are dropped. Passing an owner by value moves it instead of copying it,
    so that what it owns has exactly one owner. Since line 138, v holds nothing.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    If eat only needs to look at the value, change its parameter to *owned[L]
    and pass a pointer:
        eat(&v)
    If this is the last use of v, move it before line 138, where v still holds
    its value.
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3301" for a longer explanation)
